From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:15:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Transcribe dictation in the language picked on the watch

consnop's patched PebbleOS lets the dictation screen pick the spoken
language (SK / EN / DE). It sends the ISO 639-1 code with the session
setup as voice attribute 0x40, and sends voice command 0x40 (session id
plus the same attribute) when the pick changes during the recording.

VoiceService reads both; the coordinator keeps the session's language,
updated by changes for its session id until the session ends, and hands
the provider a getter it reads once the recording has ended.
TranscriptionProvider gains an overload taking that getter, defaulting to
the old call, so providers that ignore the language are unchanged. The
hybrid path (local whisper and the self-hosted server) uses the watch's
language over the spoken language setting; Rebble's ASR and the local
fallback in the Rebble modes keep their own handling.

Firmware without the patch sends neither, so the setting applies as
before.

